From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 06:35:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 6/8] arm64: dts: qcom: kaanapali-oneplus-iceland: let the
 GMU's suppliers sync

No driver binds the GMU device: msm reaches it through
of_find_device_by_node() from a6xx_gmu_init(). fw_devlink therefore keeps
its device links to gcc, gpucc and gxclkctl in the "available" state, and
the genpd sync_state() of those three clock controllers runs only when the
deferred probe timeout forces it, about 16 s into every boot. Until then
the GDSCs that were on at handoff (GPU CX, GX and the unvoted gcc ones)
cannot power off, and the log shows the three sync_state timeouts.

Mark the three controllers as post-init providers of the GMU, so that
fw_devlink makes no device link for them and their sync_state() runs once
the bound consumers have probed. The GMU still enables its clocks and
power domains explicitly before it boots.

This is a local workaround until "drm/msm: Attach a driver to GMU" lands
upstream; drop it then.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts
index 7ac40870b..636041daa 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts
@@ -1168,6 +1168,16 @@ csiphy5_out: endpoint {
 	};
 };
 
+&gmu {
+	/*
+	 * No driver binds the GMU device (msm reaches it through
+	 * of_find_device_by_node()), so fw_devlink holds the sync_state of
+	 * gcc, gpucc and gxclkctl until the deferred probe timeout. Local
+	 * workaround until "drm/msm: Attach a driver to GMU" is merged.
+	 */
+	post-init-providers = <&gcc>, <&gpucc>, <&gxclkctl>;
+};
+
 &gpu_opp_table {
 	/*
 	 * The Pad 4's stock GPU levels (qcom,gpu-pwrlevels for speed bin 0xfc):
